        "id": 2021475
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-10T11:15:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which usecase needs this API?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e5352d8_78884b4a",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-11T20:15:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current usecase is to access keys that should only be accessible by specific entities (KeyMint\u0027s Key Agreement Key is an example). That being said, we would like to remove this function from the specification; so we are exploring ways of implementing the currently needed functionality in other ways.",
      "parentUuid": "941db4db_36e6aeae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33018424_3ae98000",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 2021475
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T05:59:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Acknowledged",
      "parentUuid": "9e5352d8_78884b4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07160dd7_9b47f9ef",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T01:23:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can any key be exported? Does the key have to be configured as exportable during generation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d00b05c_ac260241",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T18:47:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes; there are a set of [permissions on the key policy](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/2954695/14/staging/security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/KeyPolicy.aidl#42) set during key creation that specify which (if any) key lifetime type can wrap a key. If none of these permissions are set, the key cannot be exported.",
      "parentUuid": "07160dd7_9b47f9ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f13f7709_1682b6fe",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 150,
      "author": {
        "id": 2021475
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-10T11:15:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently GPCA supports HMAC key size \u003d\u003d digest size only.\nFor example HMAC_SHA256 key size \u003d 32 bytes. We cannot generate a 4B HMAC key for example.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60a5aa98_3f6ee6ee",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 150,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-11T20:15:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. I think in that case (GPCA) the function would need to return an error if a different size is requested (or have an internal workaround on the implementation), but in the general case, HMAC keys can have an arbitrary size. Do you foresee an issue with this approach?",
      "parentUuid": "f13f7709_1682b6fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a80a950_5807cd16",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 150,
      "author": {
        "id": 2021475
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T05:59:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes HMAC keys in general can have any arbitrary size.\n\nBut for the cases of key generation would it be acceptable to let the key size be decided by hardware and remove the key_size argument altogether?",
      "parentUuid": "60a5aa98_3f6ee6ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "409944e6_9c991d49",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IHwCryptoKeyGeneration.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 150,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T17:08:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do need to be able to specify the key length to be able to cover all use cases (we know that at least KeyMint requires to have arbitrary sizes for HMAC keys). This specific field is a nullable, so I have added to the docstring that it can be left as null to use the implementation default key size for HMAC keys. Will this work for you?",
      "parentUuid": "8a80a950_5807cd16",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "d55d603c6352ebb30264f52edca1db891f6f88d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
